; Start the second pass over a stored order
;
; Reached from #R$8315 when the end of a phrase is met while InputFromOrder
; is 0 (seen with SAY TO THORIN "GIVE MAP TO ME", frame 14895 of verbs.txt).
; Keeps D, DE, BC, IY and ParserWordCount, moves IY back one phrase record
; ($18 bytes) and re-enters the dispatcher at #R$758A with InputFromOrder = 1.
; #R$8315 then stores the phrases parsed since in the order slots at $B738.
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; D Class nibble of the last word, kept in PicVar2 ($824F)
; IY Phrase record being built
@label=BeginOrderPass
c$82FD LD A,D
 $82FE LD ($824F),A     ; kept in PicVar2 ($824F)
 $8301 PUSH DE
 $8302 PUSH BC
 $8303 PUSH IY
 $8305 LD A,($B706)
 $8308 LD ($8250),A     ; ParserWordCount kept in PicVar3 ($8250)
 $830B LD DE,$FFE8      ; IY back one phrase record
 $830E ADD IY,DE
 $8310 LD A,$01         ; A=1 becomes InputFromOrder at #R$758A
 $8312 JP $758A
